  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **Fixed: `Be` threw on two equal tuples holding an item that can't be compared.** A `ValueTuple` or a `Tuple` implements `IComparable` whatever its items, and its `CompareTo` throws an `ArgumentException`, \"At least one object must implement IComparable\", for an item that implements none, such as a class with value equality alone. `Be` now compares a tuple with `CompareTo` only when each of its items can be compared, and by its equality alone otherwise. Equal tuples holding the same instances passed before, which hid the bug until a tuple held an equal but distinct instance, such as one read back from a file.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Internals.SystemCE 0.10.0-internal (was 0.9.0-internal), Compze.Threading 0.13.0-alpha (was 0.12.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
